  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 124 PM CDT Thu Jun 18 2026\n\nRain and thunderstorm chances should start to decrease Friday night \nand Saturday morning as the initial upper-level wave will move \neastward and the surface front washes out. Southerly return flow on \nSaturday will feed a hot and humid airmass back into west central \nTexas. This will allow skies to clear out and temperatures to climb \nback into the low 90s. Weak ridging aloft will develop across the \nregion for Sunday and Monday, followed by northwest flow aloft for \nTuesday and Wednesday.  As a result, hot and dry conditions will \nreturn for the start of the week with temperatures approaching \ntriple digits. By the middle of next week chances will increase for \nevening and overnight thunderstorms, mainly across the Big Country, \nas models show another cold front dropping into the Southern\nPlains.",
